meta {
  name: 27 Transfer - Picked Up
  type: http
  seq: 27
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/transfers/{{transferId}}/pick-up
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "pickedUpBy": "Amit Driver"
  }
}

tests {
  test("transition applied (or rejected by the state machine)", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.be.oneOf([200, 201, 422]);
  });
}

docs {
  Picked Up (§B.11.1) — **In-Transit → Picked Up**. Records `pickedUpBy` +
  `pickedUpAt`. Bulk: `POST /accession/transfers/bulk/pick-up` with `ids[]`.

  Cancelled order: a single call on a transfer whose order was cancelled is refused
  (409 `TRANSFER_ORDER_CANCELLED`). In a bulk call with `skipInvalid: true` that transfer is
  SKIPPED instead (listed in `skipped` with `code: TRANSFER_ORDER_CANCELLED` and the reason);
  the other transfers are done. Bulk calls work through the ids in sorted order (so two
  overlapping bulk calls cannot deadlock); `succeeded` / `skipped` come back in the order
  the ids were sent.

  **Logistics rule.** Picking up an INTERNAL transfer that is still `IN_TRANSIT` with no
  logistics type is refused: 422 `TRANSFER_LOGISTICS_MISSING` ("Logistics type not set by
  the sending branch yet."). The same on `transfers/bulk/pick-up`: with `skipInvalid: true`
  the transfer is listed under `skipped` with that code and reason; without it the whole
  call is refused. Receive and Accept can only follow Pick Up, so they cannot run ahead.
  Transfers already Picked Up or later are not affected.

  **An OUTSOURCE transfer must be assigned before it moves.** A sample can be outsourced with no center and no
  logistics type (both optional, set later with Assign Center), but such a transfer can not be Picked Up / Received /
  Accepted: Pick Up needs a center AND a logistics type, Receive and Accept need the center. Otherwise 422
  `TRANSFER_OUTSOURCE_NOT_ASSIGNED`, "This outsource transfer has no center and no logistics type yet. Use Assign
  Center in In-House Orders to set it, then try again." (naming only what is missing; `details.missing` lists it).
  Nothing is changed. A bulk call with `skipInvalid` skips that transfer with this code and reason. This is the
  outsource counterpart of an INTERNAL transfer needing a destination branch and a logistics type; Forward (EXTERNAL)
  is not covered, and Repeat / Reject are not guarded. The free-text Update Status is not affected.
}
